  "text": "That\u2019s a wonderful idea for Mother\u2019s Day! A classic breakfast omelette is a simple, comforting, and delicious way to surprise your mom. Here\u2019s how to make a classic breakfast omelette:\n\n---\n\n### **Ingredients** (Serves 1 or 2):\n- 2 large eggs\n- 1/4 cup milk or heavy cream (for fluffiness)\n- Salt and pepper to taste\n- 1 tablespoon butter or oil\n- Optional: chopped herbs (like parsley or chives), shredded cheese, or cooked bacon or ham\n\n---\n\n### **Instructions**:\n\n1. **Crack the Eggs**: In a bowl, crack two eggs and whisk them together with a fork or a hand mixer until well mixed. Add the milk or cream and a pinch of salt and pepper.\n\n2. **Heat the Pan**: In a non-stick skillet over medium heat, melt the butter or heat the oil.\n\n3. **Cook the Omelette**: Pour the egg mixture into the pan. Let it cook undisturbed for about 2\u20133 minutes, or until the edges are set and the top is still slightly runny.\n\n4. **Add Fillings (Optional)**: If using cheese, bacon, or herbs, add them to one half of the omelette. Use a spatula to fold the other half over the fillings.\n\n5. **Finish Cooking**: Let it cook for another minute or two, just until the cheese is melted or the fillings are fully cooked.\n\n6. **Serve**: Slide the omelette onto a plate, and serve warm. You can top it with a little more cheese or herbs if you like.\n\n---\n\n### **Pro Tips**:\n- For extra fluffiness, use heavy cream instead of milk.\n- If you're using cheese, choose a mild one like Swiss or mozzarella.\n- Use a non-stick pan to prevent the eggs from sticking.\n- A little butter in the pan adds a rich, buttery flavor.\n\n---\n\nThis simple and elegant dish is a great surprise, easy to make, and totally customizable. Your mom will definitely appreciate the thoughtful gesture! \ud83c\udf73\ud83d\udc96\n\nIf you'd like, I can also help you come up with a fun, surprise breakfast menu for Mother\u2019s Day!",
